# .adl-ignore file
# This file specifies which files should not be overwritten during generation operations.
# Files listed here typically contain implementations that users have completed.
#
# Patterns supported:
# - Exact file names: tools/agent_tool.go
# - Wildcards: *.go
# - Directory patterns: tools/*
# - Directories: build/
# - Comments: lines starting with #

tools/echo.go
tools/delay.go
tools/error.go
tools/random_data.go
tools/validate.go
tools/simulate_tool_call.go

# Skill playbooks are hand-authored; the generator only seeds blank
# scaffolds. Protect the whole skills/ tree so regen never clobbers
# the bodies (or any bundled scripts/templates/resources).
skills/

# Hand-maintained but kept in sync with the generated template. main.go
# carries TWO deliberate deviations from `adl generate` output, each fenced
# with BEGIN/END comments in the file:
#   1. It wires internal/mock.NewMockLLMClient instead of the generator's
#      default OpenAI-compatible client (mock-agent's whole purpose is to run
#      without real LLM credentials). This is also why the file must be ignored
#      at all: the generated template hardcodes
#      server.NewOpenAICompatibleLLMClient with no seam to inject a custom
#      client.
#   2. It keeps the explicit OpenTelemetry wiring (otel.NewOpenTelemetry +
#      WithTelemetry + ShutDown) that the v0.51.0 template dropped in favor of
#      A2AServerBuilder.Build()'s internal init. mock-agent owns its telemetry
#      lifecycle on purpose, so we re-apply this by hand.
# When bumping the ADL CLI, regenerate into a scratch dir and re-apply just
# those two fenced blocks (see the header note in main.go). Dropping this entry
# entirely is blocked on an adl-cli extension point for a custom LLM client
# (tracked upstream) - until then, keeping it synced by hand is how we pick up
# template fixes like the OTel service.name propagation.
main.go

# Hand-authored example stacks (docker-compose, collector configs, docs)
# that live outside the generated surface.
examples/

# Add your own files to ignore here:
# my-custom-file.go
# config/secrets.yaml

